  "tagline": "A single C++ binary for streaming SQL, built on ClickHouse's engine with streams and windows.",
  "description": "Proton is Timeplus's open-source streaming SQL engine, derived from a single-node ClickHouse codebase and extended with a native stream storage, watermarks, tumble/hop/session windows, changelog streams and incremental materialized views. It reads and writes Kafka, Redpanda, Pulsar, ClickHouse, Postgres/MySQL and S3/Iceberg, and ships as one binary with no JVM or ZooKeeper. Proton 3.0 (late 2025) brought large performance gains, and patch releases continue. The commercial Timeplus Enterprise adds clustering, a UI and alerting.",
